UID:state-pte-west-virginia-2025-03-17@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T115707Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:West Virginia: SPF-100 due
DESCRIPTION:West Virginia S-corp/partnership return due the 15th day of the
  3rd month after year-end. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited sou
 rce states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing 
 the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consis
 tent with every other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a wee
 kend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Mon
 tana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-
 universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the next busines
 s day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2
 026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift
  convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that t
 his specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | West
  Virginia S-corp/partnership return due the 15th day of the 3rd month after
  year-end. File Form SPF-100EXT by the original due date\; a federal extens
 ion carries over automatically to WV. Correction (this rebuild session): th
 e cited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without 
 addressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sun
 day. Consistent with every other state in this data set that explicitly con
 firms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Del
 aware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and wit
 h the near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the n
 ext business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted M
 arch 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the ge
 neral shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirma
 tion that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transpare
 ncy. | Authority: West Virginia State Tax Department\, fetched this session
  (2018-edition instructions\; the 15th-day-of-3rd-month rule and the federa
 l-extension-carryover rule are long-standing and not year-specific): "Any S
  Corporation or Partnership granted an extension of time to file their fede
 ral return is granted the same extension of time to file their West Virgini
 a return." | Source: https://tax.wv.gov/Documents/TaxForms/2018/spf100.inst
 ructions.pdf | This date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not ref
 lect a later-announced change\; confirm against the cited source before rel
 ying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
